\f1\fs22 He fled into the building, away from the world, leaving a trail of bloody shoe prints on the polished floor\'97except for the spot where he\'92d tripped over an automated cleaner polishing the floor. He fled toward imagined safety, in a sequestered part of Starborne One to which it seemed only he had access. Or perhaps the building only executed naked alcoholics; Chanta could not be certain of the building\'92s ethics or morality.\
Behind a stand of tropical palms arranged around a water feature, Chanta encountered an elevator lobby with two pairs of sparkling jewel-encrusted doors. Worse than their gaudiness: they were shut, and staying that way, with no apparent calling panel. Perhaps Chanta was meant to simply walk through the elevator doors too\'97he was quickly becoming accustomed to his new superpower. But what if there was no elevator car awaiting, and he fell down the elevator shaft? Perhaps he would not go splat at the bottom, but would pass through there also, all the way to the Cloudborne ground and travel on until he was cooked by the heat of the inner earth.\
None of those happened because, before too much time had passed, one pair of doors opened, admitted Chanta and, with the silent ease and grace of expensive engineering, whisked him to a three-storey penthouse atop the tower.\
A young King Creole Series ELVIS stood at ease in the egress from the elevator lobby, feet wide apart, hands clasped behind his back. He wore an impeccably tailored velvet coat that accentuated his shoulders and narrowed his waist; a gold, angular brooch pinned to a lapel; a tastefully lustrous buttoned-up purple vest; a crisp high-collared white shirt; an aquamarine cravat; white gloves; breeches; and polished, buckled shoes.\
\'93Greetings, sir,\'94 the ELVIS said. \'93My name is Fisher. I am delighted to finally meet you. We have been anticipating your arrival.\'94\
\'93Have you?\'94 Chanta asked. He suspected the ELVIS might be blocking his passage. Warily, Chanta stole a couple more paces away from the elevator, and heard its door close behind. \'93Have we met?\'94\
\'93No, sir.\'94\
\'93Then why are you happy to meet me?\'94 Chanta could count, on one hand with a thumb and a pinky amputated, the number of people who might be genuinely happy to see him. With sadness, he recalled another finger had been amputated: Halo. He may have been a psychopathic, misogynistic serial killer who tried to off Sarah, but Halo was still Chanta\'92s friend. Or had been. \'93What am I to you?\'94\
\'93You are the one and lawful heir to Jamison Hardy,\'94 Fisher answered formally, his chin rising a fraction.\
Chanta\'92s mind seized up in a fashion only hard liquor could re-lubricate. \'93I\'92m the what now?\'94\
\'93You are the\'97\'94\
\'93Jamison Hardy? The once richest person in the world\'85 that Jamison Hardy?\'94\
\'93Yes, sir. I am sure you noticed your penthouse sits atop this, his eponymous tower.\'94\
\'93Well, I suppose\'97wait\'85 my penthouse?\'94\
\'93Yes, sir.\'94\
Chanta put his bloody hand to his forehead and worried some wrinkles into it as he tried figuring out what the actual tax was going on. \'93You don\'92t know me\'85 how\'97how do you know I\'92m Hardy\'92s heir?\'94\
\'93You opened the Rose Door, sir.\'94\
\'93The Rose Door? You mean the disappearing wall? I didn\'92t do anything.\'94\
\'93More specifically, your DNA opened the door.\'94 When Chanta looked at him blankly, Fisher added, \'93The Rose Door sniffed your DNA as soon as you rubbed your nose against it.\'94\
\'93I see.\'94 Actually Chanta didn\'92t see; his mind was foggier than the Layer after New Year\'92s Eve fireworks. \'93But, Danny\'85 may I call you Danny?\'94\
The King Creole Series ELVIS shifted uncomfortably on his feet. \'93I would prefer Fisher, sir.\'94\
\'93How can you be sure, Fisher, I\'92m the only descendant? There could be thousands of us.\'94\
\'93Mr Hardy enjoyed good competition\'85 survival of the fittest and all that.\'94\
Chanta never considered he might be the fittest at anything.\
\'93In any case,\'94 Fisher continued, \'93you\'92re the first to have opened the Rose Door. You win.\'94\
